        <mxCell id="HQQ4V66wD_OCbyy4vYDD-69" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;text-align: left; margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;Key Generation For Short Url&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;div&gt;All keys for short urls will be pre-generated by key generation service (KGS).&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Key length is 6 chars. Using base64 encoding system, I can get: 64^6 = 68,7 billion keys&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;After key retrieved, it will be moved to deletedKeys.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;I&#39;ll run N number of instances of this service for redundancy, in case one service goes down, or if there is very high load.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Also we cache N number of urls in redis, so clients can get key immediately. There can be a situation when we lose some keys if redis goes down. However it is okay in our case, since we have way more unique keys than we need.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;However we want to replicate our data for fault tolerance and read latency.&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="310" width="780" x="600" y="440" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="HQQ4V66wD_OCbyy4vYDD-70" parent="1" style="shape=table;startSize=30;container=1;collapsible=1;childLayout=tableLayout;fixedRows=1;rowLines=0;fontStyle=1;align=center;resizeLast=1;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="keys" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="90" width="180" x="620" y="545" as="geometry" />
